            <h2>4. How Marathi Text To Speech Works</h2>
            <p>Understanding the basic mechanics of text-to-speech (TTS) helps you get better results. You do not need to be a software engineer, but knowing the workflow makes a difference.</p>
            <p>When you input text, the system first performs language processing. It breaks down the sentences into individual words and understands the grammar. It identifies if a sentence is a statement or a question. This is crucial for determining how the voice should sound.</p>
            <p>Next is pronunciation handling. Marathi has specific sounds that do not exist in English. The AI engine uses a massive dictionary of phonetic sounds mapped to the Devanagari script. It knows how to combine consonants and vowels correctly.</p>
            <p>Then comes voice synthesis. Instead of stitching together pre-recorded words (which sounds robotic), modern neural AI generates the sound waves dynamically. It predicts how a human would transition smoothly from one sound to the next.</p>
            <p>Finally, the audio generation phase outputs the final digital file. This file contains the complete waveform of the spoken words, ready for you to download and use.</p>

